> parse 2x^2 + 3x - 1
(((2 * (x ^ 2)) + (3 * x)) - 1)
> parse 1/2x
(1 / (2 * x))
  note: 1/2x read as 1/(2x); write (1/...)... for the other reading
> parse -x^2
(-(x ^ 2))
> parse sin x^2 + cos 2x
(sin((x ^ 2)) + cos((2 * x)))
> parse sin x cos x
(sin(x) * cos(x))
> parse |x - |y||
abs((x - abs(y)))
> parse a < b < c
((a < b) && (b < c))
  note: chained comparison read as a conjunction
> parse x(y + 1)
(x * (y + 1))
  note: x(...) read as multiplication: x is not a function
> parse xy + 1
((x * y) + 1)
  note: 'xy' read as x*y (single-letter variables)
> parse 2pi r
(6.283185307 * r)
> parse x² + y³
((x ^ 2) + (y ^ 3))
> parse a & b == c
((a & b) == c)
  note: bitwise operators bind tighter than comparisons here (unlike C): read as ((a & b) == c)
> parse x = 0 ? 1 : 2
((x == 0) ? 1 : 2)
  note: '=' inside an expression read as '=='
> 1/2 + 1/3
0.833333
> 7/2
3.5
> 2^10
1024
> sqrt(2)
1.41421
> f(n: u8) = sqrt(n)
  note: sqrt of the integer n read as floor square root isqrt(); write sqrt(real(n)) for the real one
> show f
f(n: u8) = isqrt(n)
  -> u8
> g(x) = x xor 3
  note: x has no type: inferred int from the integer operations in the body
> show g
g(x: int) = x xor 3
  -> int
> h = a*b + c
  note: h has free variables: defined as h(a, b, c)
> show h
h(a: real, b: real, c: real) = a*b + c
  -> real
